# Code ownership for behunintree.com
#
# The ruleset on main has require_code_owner_review enabled, so a PR touching
# any path owned here cannot merge without review from that owner.
#
# Ben has write access because personal (non-organization) GitHub repos offer
# exactly one collaborator level. This file is how the content-vs-code line is
# drawn in a repo that cannot express it as a permission.

# Default: everything belongs to Blake unless carved out below.
*                       @lewisbwl

# Structure, styling, behavior, and build. This is the line crossed in PR #2,
# which touched styles.css alongside its content changes.
/*.html                 @lewisbwl
/styles.css             @lewisbwl
/script.js              @lewisbwl
/build.js               @lewisbwl

# Deploy and security configuration. The strict CSP here is what keeps pasted
# markup from becoming executable, so it is not a content decision.
/netlify.toml           @lewisbwl
/_headers               @lewisbwl
/_redirects             @lewisbwl
/robots.txt             @lewisbwl
/sitemap.xml            @lewisbwl
/.github/               @lewisbwl

# Optimized image derivatives are generated, not authored. Source photos are
# reviewed before they become derivatives.
/img/                   @lewisbwl

# Once the generator exists, content/ is where Ben works and this becomes the
# one path he owns outright. Left commented until that directory is real, so
# the rule cannot silently match nothing.
# /content/             @bensbehunin @lewisbwl
